"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The project has progressed through several phases, including design, testing, and development (led by Omar Jensen), with a prototype for secure file sharing successfully tested ahead of schedule. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and the upcoming user interface enhancements planned for October. The project team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. There are also early-stage discussions regarding a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Budget updates indicate an initial allocation of $500,000, adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, and subsequently approved by the executive board for $2M to cover all research, development, and marketing phases, with detailed allocations to be discussed on August 1st."
